#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, fuzzy, no-wrap
#| msgid "This course covers several approaches to matrix diagonalization using quantum computers."
msgid "Explore quantum approaches to matrix diagonalization, including VQE, QKD, SKD and variations of these."
msgstr "Kursus ini mencakup beberapa pendekatan untuk diagonalisasi matriks menggunakan komputer kuantum."

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overview"
msgstr "Gambaran Umum"

#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overview {#overview}"
msgstr "Gambaran Umum {#overview}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![\"Hero image\"](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/hero.avif)\n"
msgstr "![\"Gambar hero\"](/learning/images/courses/quantum-diagonalization-algorithms/hero.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This course provides an overview of several approaches to quantum diagonalization. Some background is provided on the classical methods that are used, or that motivated the quantum algorithms. The content then steps through the implementation of the quantum algorithms on real quantum computers. There is substantial discussion of what factors determine the scaling of approaches using classical and quantum algorithms.\n"
msgstr "Kursus ini memberikan gambaran umum tentang beberapa pendekatan untuk diagonalisasi kuantum. Beberapa latar belakang disediakan tentang metode klasik yang digunakan, atau yang memotivasi algoritma kuantum. Konten kemudian melalui implementasi algoritma kuantum pada komputer kuantum nyata. Ada diskusi substantif tentang faktor apa yang menentukan penskalaan pendekatan menggunakan algoritma klasik dan kuantum.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Recommended background {#recommended-background}"
msgstr "Latar belakang yang disarankan {#recommended-background}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This course is intended for individuals who have some experience with quantum computing and want to leverage its power in matrix diagonalization.\n"
msgstr "Kursus ini ditujukan untuk individu yang memiliki pengalaman dengan komputasi kuantum dan ingin memanfaatkan kekuatannya dalam diagonalisasi matriks.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We recommend that learners complete the following prerequisites prior to this course:\n"
msgstr "Kami menyarankan para pelajar untuk menyelesaikan prasyarat berikut sebelum kursus ini:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set up your local environment by following along with the [Get started](/guides/) guide in our documentation page.\n"
msgstr "Siapkan lingkungan lokal dengan mengikuti panduan [Get started](/guides/) dalam halaman dokumentasi kami.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "For deeper understanding of quantum information, try [Basics of Quantum Information](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information) with John Watrous.\n"
msgstr "Untuk pemahaman yang lebih mendalam tentang informasi kuantum, coba [Basics of Quantum Information](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information) bersama John Watrous.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Exam {#exam}"
msgstr "Ujian {#exam}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To earn your badge for Quantum diagonalization algorithms, take the exam at IBM&reg; Training. This exam is intended to be taken after reading the lessons in this course. After you pass the exam, you will be notified by Credly that you have earned a badge.\n"
msgstr "Untuk mendapatkan badge untuk Quantum diagonalization algorithms, ikuti ujian di IBM&reg; Training. Ujian ini dimaksudkan untuk diambil setelah membaca pelajaran dalam kursus ini. Setelah kamu lulus ujian, kamu akan diberitahu oleh Credly bahwa kamu telah mendapatkan badge.\n"

#. type: Plain text
